<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.114 pct.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 3.114 pct.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1997-05-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.0 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due August 21, 1997 was 3.114 percent, up from 3.062 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.1 billion of 182-day T-bills due November 20, 1997 was 3.462 percent, up from 3.431 percent last week, and on C$1.0 billion of 357-day T-bills due May 14, 1998 was 3.892 percent, down from 3.966 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$550 million three-month, C$125 million six-month and C$100 million one-year bills. It holds C$625 million of C$5.5 billion bills due May 29.</p>
